{"id":"drafts--telecom-network-function--examples--cbom-open5gs-sepp-fail-referencepoint","file":"cbom-open5gs-sepp-fail-referencepoint.cdx.json","raw":"https://github.com/pkic/cbom/blob/main/drafts/telecom-network-function/examples/cbom-open5gs-sepp-fail-referencepoint.cdx.json","story":"telecom","domain":"Telecommunications","draft":true,"name":"Open5GS SEPP","version":"2.8.0","description":"The SEPP of Open5GS v2.8.0 (open5gs-seppd). Record written by the PKIC CBOM Profiles working group from the public source, not by the Open5GS maintainers.","comment":"DRAFT EXAMPLE CBOM, lifecycle stage 'implemented'. The Open5GS SEPP at v2.8.0, written from its public source by the PKIC CBOM Profiles working group. Library versions to confirm. NON-CONFORMING: N32-c does not state its reference point.","subjectType":"product","stage":"implemented","coverage":"all","fictional":false,"subjectFacts":[{"name":"absent:management-interface","values":["configured-out-of-band"]},{"name":"absent:vulnerability-statements","values":["not-published"]}],"identifier":"pkg:github/open5gs/open5gs@v2.8.0","interfaces":[{"ref":"n32c","name":"N32-c: N32 handshake between SEPPs (HTTPS)","type":"interconnect","attributes":[{"name":"interfaceType","values":["interconnect"]},{"name":"protocol","values":["TLS"]},{"name":"protocolVersion","values":["1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchange","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"encryption","values":["AES-256-GCM"]},{"name":"authentication","values":["deployment-defined"]},{"name":"protocolVersionsSupported","values":["1.2","1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchangeSupported","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"authenticationSupported","values":["ECDSA","RSA"]},{"name":"endpointRole:client","values":["endpoint:sepp"]},{"name":"endpointRole:server","values":["endpoint:peer-sepp"]},{"name":"algorithmSelection","values":["Certificate and key from the 'tls' section of sepp.yaml; client certificate verification is off unless 'verify_client' is set"]},{"name":"integrationConstraints","values":["The server context (lib/sbi/nghttp2-server.c) allows TLS 1.0 to 1.3 and sets the group list to P-256 only, so the server negotiates ECDHE on P-256 whatever the client offers. OpenSSL 3 refuses TLS 1.0 and 1.1 at its default security level. TLS 1.2 suites are ECDHE-ECDSA and ECDHE-RSA with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, and DHE-RSA with AES-GCM; TLS 1.3 suites are the OpenSSL defaults, with server preference. The client side (lib/sbi/client.c) uses libcurl with OpenSSL and its default groups. There is no setting for the group list. The SEPP advertises TLS as its only N32-f security capability. Library version from an Ubuntu 24.04 build; to confirm."]},{"name":"keysStoredIn","values":["sto-keys"]},{"name":"defaultState","values":["enabled"]}],"purposes":{},"endpoints":[]},{"ref":"n32f","name":"N32-f: forwarded messages between SEPPs (HTTPS)","type":"interconnect","attributes":[{"name":"interfaceType","values":["interconnect"]},{"name":"protocol","values":["TLS"]},{"name":"protocolVersion","values":["1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchange","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"encryption","values":["AES-256-GCM"]},{"name":"authentication","values":["deployment-defined"]},{"name":"protocolVersionsSupported","values":["1.2","1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchangeSupported","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"authenticationSupported","values":["ECDSA","RSA"]},{"name":"endpointRole:client","values":["endpoint:sepp"]},{"name":"endpointRole:server","values":["endpoint:peer-sepp"]},{"name":"algorithmSelection","values":["A separate listener and certificate may be set in the 'n32f' section"]},{"name":"integrationConstraints","values":["PRINS is not implemented: N32-f is protected by TLS only. The server context (lib/sbi/nghttp2-server.c) allows TLS 1.0 to 1.3 and sets the group list to P-256 only, so the server negotiates ECDHE on P-256 whatever the client offers. OpenSSL 3 refuses TLS 1.0 and 1.1 at its default security level. TLS 1.2 suites are ECDHE-ECDSA and ECDHE-RSA with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, and DHE-RSA with AES-GCM; TLS 1.3 suites are the OpenSSL defaults, with server preference. The client side (lib/sbi/client.c) uses libcurl with OpenSSL and its default groups. There is no setting for the group list. Library version from an Ubuntu 24.04 build; to confirm."]},{"name":"referencePoint","values":["n32-f"]},{"name":"governingSpecification","values":["TS 33.501 13.1 and 13.5"]},{"name":"keysStoredIn","values":["sto-keys"]},{"name":"defaultState","values":["enabled"]}],"purposes":{},"endpoints":[]},{"ref":"sbi","name":"Service-based interface to the operator's network functions","type":"service","attributes":[{"name":"interfaceType","values":["service"]},{"name":"protocol","values":["TLS"]},{"name":"protocolVersion","values":["1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchange","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"encryption","values":["AES-256-GCM"]},{"name":"authentication","values":["deployment-defined"]},{"name":"protocolVersionsSupported","values":["1.2","1.3"]},{"name":"keyExchangeSupported","values":["ECDH-P256"]},{"name":"authenticationSupported","values":["ECDSA","RSA"]},{"name":"endpointRole:client","values":["endpoint:nf-consumer"]},{"name":"endpointRole:server","values":["endpoint:sepp"]},{"name":"algorithmSelection","values":["The scheme is set per server in the 'sbi' section: 'http' or 'https'"]},{"name":"integrationConstraints","values":["The shipped configuration uses HTTP without TLS on the SBI. With 'https', the same TLS context as N32 applies. The server context (lib/sbi/nghttp2-server.c) allows TLS 1.0 to 1.3 and sets the group list to P-256 only, so the server negotiates ECDHE on P-256 whatever the client offers. OpenSSL 3 refuses TLS 1.0 and 1.1 at its default security level. TLS 1.2 suites are ECDHE-ECDSA and ECDHE-RSA with AES-GCM or ChaCha20-Poly1305, and DHE-RSA with AES-GCM; TLS 1.3 suites are the OpenSSL defaults, with server preference. The client side (lib/sbi/client.c) uses libcurl with OpenSSL and its default groups. There is no setting for the group list. Library version from an Ubuntu 24.04 build; to confirm."]},{"name":"referencePoint","values":["sbi"]},{"name":"governingSpecification","values":["TS 33.501 13.1"]},{"name":"keysStoredIn","values":["sto-keys"]},{"name":"defaultState","values":["disabled"]}],"purposes":{},"endpoints":[]},{"ref":"sto-keys","name":"Private keys, certificates and CA certificates (PEM files)","type":"storage","attributes":[{"name":"interfaceType","values":["storage"]},{"name":"encryption","values":["none"]},{"name":"keyWrapping","values":["none"]},{"name":"integrationConstraints","values":["Read from the file paths in sepp.yaml at start-up. Protection of the files is left to the platform."]},{"name":"referencePoint","values":["not-a-reference-point"]},{"name":"defaultState","values":["enabled"]}],"purposes":{},"endpoints":[]}],"references":[{"context":"sbom","type":"bom","url":"urn:cdx:5e990002-0000-4000-8000-0000000000b0/1","comment":"Companion SBOM: examples/context/open5gs-sepp-2.8.0-sbom.cdx.json.","hashed":true},{"context":"advisories","type":"advisories","url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/security/advisories","comment":"The project's published security advisories.","hashed":false},{"context":"configuration-guidance","type":"configuration","url":"https://open5gs.org/open5gs/docs/","comment":"The project's documentation, including the TLS settings in sepp.yaml.","hashed":false},{"context":"vcs","type":"vcs","url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/tree/v2.8.0","comment":"The source the record was written from.","hashed":false}],"profiles":[{"tag":"telecom-network-function","title":"Telecom Network Function (Example, draft)","version":"0.1-draft","draft":true,"verdict":"does-not-conform","failing":["n32c/telecom-network-function#I1"],"gapAnalysis":false,"with":[],"report":{"product":[["pass","MUST","interface-disclosure#P1","Product declares at least one cryptographic interface","4 interface(s) declared"],["pass","MUST","interface-disclosure#P2","Product declares at lea